# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Atmos Weather — environment configuration template
# Copy to ".env" for local development:  cp .env.example .env
# NEVER commit a real key. ".env" is git-ignored.
# All variables are OPTIONAL — the app runs on free public endpoints by default.
# Note: Vite exposes VITE_* variables to the browser. They are NOT secrets.
# Any key that must stay secret belongs behind a backend proxy, not here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional: Gemini API key placeholder for future AI insight experiments.
# Restrict the key by HTTP referrer/domain in Google Cloud Console.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Production scale (1000+ users) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The free Open-Meteo endpoints have daily call limits. For production traffic,
# switch to the commercial customer endpoints and provide your API key:
# VITE_OPEN_METEO_API_KEY=
# VITE_OPEN_METEO_FORECAST_URL=https://customer-api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast
# VITE_OPEN_METEO_GEOCODING_URL=https://customer-geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search
# VITE_OPEN_METEO_AIR_QUALITY_URL=https://customer-air-quality-api.open-meteo.com/v1/air-quality
# VITE_OPEN_METEO_ARCHIVE_URL=https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/archive

# Optional: override the RainViewer metadata endpoint.
# VITE_RAINVIEWER_API_URL=https://api.rainviewer.com/public/weather-maps.json
